uid "1d58c576-c6e6-5e37-8883-0155d746b92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556498} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc48711-9294-5620-8821-e5c664e49e7f" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3412a484-45d8-574d-9d62-4ede649dfd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556541} {:answer/id #uuid "35c4e0e7-1d76-539c-97b6-f431a62e393c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556546} {:answer/id #uuid "55d344b2-0d9d-5c9e-9649-438f542aaff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556628} {:answer/id #uuid "83cd1bb7-6b3e-5f38-831e-6c8449b88613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556738} {:answer/id #uuid "d1852c5e-8a51-5e17-8a30-b0f014c72c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55d344b2-0d9d-5c9e-9649-438f542aaff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d735f931-6366-5aec-9f2f-070c16532ce5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79cf6220-8640-5993-92c2-8195fa289578" :question/math-academy-id "q-335009" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-2x+3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=4y-5xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\,0]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=-2x+3xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=4y-5xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2x+3xy)=-2+3y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2x+3xy)=3x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4y-5xy)=-5y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y-5xy)=4-5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y & 3x \\\\ -5y & 4-5x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3(0) & 3(0) \\\\ -5(0) & 4-5(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2\\text{ and }{\\lambda }_{2}=4.$ Since eigenvalues are real with opposite signs, our equilibrium is $\\text{an unstable}$ $\\text{saddle}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c9c2220-030e-5418-915c-e34d7962c077" :knowledge-point/title "Analyzing a Solution of the Lotka-Volterra Model Given the Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f2b091a-08be-5090-bccc-dabfbfd338d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370295} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc19115-d3ea-57bc-80f0-ef8b433ebf1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc19115-d3ea-57bc-80f0-ef8b433ebf1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370296} :answer-field/id #uuid "84e7c980-e92a-5a03-bd66-8798970ea529" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f09f1710-6357-5cc6-92c0-d0bd21e35f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "circles around" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370298} {:answer/id #uuid "00ba3cf3-b8b0-5b9f-8167-f01c398804e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "approaches" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f09f1710-6357-5cc6-92c0-d0bd21e35f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "circles around" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370298} :answer-field/id #uuid "b563c118-2623-59c6-866f-660c566bc30e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f0de15d-5728-526f-9e45-b96867986aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370301} {:answer/id #uuid "28f0b35b-80c2-5312-9706-767f7322ce5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f0de15d-5728-526f-9e45-b96867986aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370301} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ae8e29-fc3b-5839-8db5-0e88f2110106" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370300} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91874472-a3a6-521b-9d88-799d0070be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the nonzero equilibrium" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370304} {:answer/id #uuid "d48743c2-c632-5562-8a0e-95eceb275aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the point of inflection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370305} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6e781c-8489-5f0a-91d9-39d3d5319fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91874472-a3a6-521b-9d88-799d0070be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the nonzero equilibrium" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370304} :answer-field/id #uuid "04cbcbb8-c325-532a-aa22-325480b13a79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fb55973-5627-54af-9b3b-ac140bde70a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-335022" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb43b1e32820fd3624ec1bc6a69055a925e16c5f416b1801acf92e3cd866e246.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait above showing a solution of a Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=6x-3xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=-9y+3xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $x=x(t),y=y(t),$ and $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are positive constants.\n\nSelect the options below that best describe the dynamics of the system from point $A$ to point $B$ on the solution.\n\n$\\,$\nThe trajectory \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$\nThe number of prey {{field-3}} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{increases}.$"}]}
